    "## Part 1 — The Business Problem\n",
    "\n",
    "A telecommunications company is losing customers to competitors — this is called **customer churn**. The company wants to understand which customers are likely to leave, so it can intervene early. Before any model can be built, the raw data must be understood, audited for quality issues, and explored.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Tasks**\n",
    "1. In 2–3 sentences, state the business problem in your own words, and propose what the target variable likely is.\n",
    "2. List 5 columns you expect to be useful predictors of churn, and 2 columns you expect to be useless as predictors — justify each choice in one line.\n",
    "3. Write down 2 questions you personally want this data to answer about customers who churn."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Answer 1:**\n",
    "\n",
    "A telecom company is experiencing customer churn — customers are leaving for competitor services. The business needs to identify which customers are at risk of churning so proactive retention strategies can be deployed. The target variable is 'Churn', a binary indicator (Yes/No) showing whether a customer has left the company.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer 2:**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Useful Predictors:**\n",
    "1. **Contract** — Customers with month-to-month contracts have lower switching costs and are more likely to leave\n",
    "2. **MonthlyCharges** — Higher bills increase dissatisfaction and churn likelihood\n",
    "3. **Tenure** — Longer-term customers develop loyalty and are less likely to churn\n",
    "4. **InternetService** — Fiber optic customers may churn more due to higher costs or service issues\n",
    "5. **TechSupport** — Customers with tech support are better supported and less likely to churn\n",
    "\n",
    "**Useless Predictors:**\n",
    "1. **customerID** — Purely an identifier, has no predictive power for churn behavior\n",
    "2. **PhoneNumber** — An identifier field with no behavioral information\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer 3:**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Question 1:** Are customers with longer tenure (loyal customers) significantly less likely to churn, and at what tenure point does loyalty become strong?\n",
    "2. **Question 2:** Which service/feature combination leads to the highest churn, and can we identify high-risk customer segments?"
   ]
