    "**Task 14 Answer:**\n",
    "\n",
    "**Is the dataset imbalanced?** YES — The dataset is moderately imbalanced:\n",
    "- No Churn: 5,174 customers (73.46%)\n",
    "- Churn: 1,869 customers (26.54%)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Problems this creates for modeling:**\n",
    "1. **Accuracy paradox:** A naive model predicting \"No Churn\" for everyone achieves 73% accuracy without learning anything\n",
    "2. **Poor minority class learning:** Models tend to underfit on the churned customer minority class\n",
    "3. **Misleading metrics:** Accuracy alone is deceptive; need Precision, Recall, F1-Score, and ROC-AUC\n",
    "\n",
    "**How to address:**\n",
    "- Use **stratified train-test split** to maintain churn ratio in both sets\n",
    "- Use appropriate **metrics**: Precision, Recall, F1-Score, ROC-AUC (NOT just accuracy)\n",
    "- Consider **class weights**: Give higher penalty to misclassifying churned customers\n",
    "- Optional: **SMOTE** or oversampling if severe imbalance (this is ~73/27 which is manageable)\n",
    "- Use **confusion matrix** to track false positives vs false negatives"
   ]
