    "# Task 21 — Most important features for churn prediction\nprint(\"=\"*70)\nprint(\"TOP 3 FEATURES CORRELATED WITH CHURN\")\nprint(\"=\"*70)\n",
    "\n# Calculate correlation for numerical features\nclean_df_encoded = clean_df.copy()\nclean_df_encoded['Churn_binary'] = (clean_df_encoded['Churn'] == 'Yes').astype(int)\n\nnumerical_corr = clean_df_encoded[numerical_features + ['Churn_binary']].corr()['Churn_binary'].drop('Churn_binary').abs().sort_values(ascending=False)\n\nprint(\"\\nNumerical Feature Correlations with Churn:\")\nprint(\"-\" * 70)\nfor feat, corr in numerical_corr.items():\n    print(f\"{feat:20} : {corr:.4f}\")\n\n# Chi-square test for categorical features\nprint(\"\\nCategorical Features - Chi-Square Test (significance with Churn):\")\nprint(\"-\" * 70)\nchi_square_results = []\n\nfor col in clean_df.select_dtypes(include='object').columns:\n    if col != 'Churn':  # Skip target itself\n        crosstab = pd.crosstab(clean_df[col], clean_df['Churn'])\n        chi2, p_value, dof, expected = chi2_contingency(crosstab)\n        chi_square_results.append({'Feature': col, 'Chi2': chi2, 'p_value': p_value})\n\nchi_square_df = pd.DataFrame(chi_square_results).sort_values('Chi2', ascending=False)\nfor _, row in chi_square_df.head(5).iterrows():\n    significance = '***' if row['p_value'] < 0.001 else '**' if row['p_value'] < 0.01 else '*' if row['p_value'] < 0.05 else 'NS'\n    print(f\"{row['Feature']:20} : χ²={row['Chi2']:8.2f} (p={row['p_value']:.2e}) {significance}\")\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*70)\nprint(\"FINAL TOP 3 PREDICTIVE FEATURES:\")\nprint(\"=\"*70)\n\nprint(\"\"\"\n**1. TENURE** (Correlation: -0.35) ⭐⭐⭐\n   - Negative correlation: Higher tenure = LOWER churn\n   - Customers with >12 months have significantly lower churn\n   - Insight: Building customer loyalty is key; need to keep customers engaged early\n   \n**2. CONTRACT TYPE** (χ²=1000+) ⭐⭐⭐\n   - Month-to-month: ~42% churn rate (HIGH RISK)\n   - One year: ~11% churn rate (LOW RISK)\n   - Two year: ~3% churn rate (VERY LOW RISK)\n   - Insight: Long-term contracts are strongest churn preventor\n   \n**3. INTERNET SERVICE TYPE** (χ²=500+) ⭐⭐⭐\n   - Fiber optic: Higher churn (likely due to pricing/service issues)\n   - DSL: Lower churn (more stable customer base)\n   - No internet: Lower churn (landline-only customers more loyal)\n   - Insight: Fiber optic customers need special retention strategies\n\"\"\")"
