    "## Part 9 — Data Leakage Awareness\n",
    "\n",
    "In Lab 3 you will train a classifier. Before that, you must check whether any column contains information that would not realistically be available at the moment of prediction — using such a column would make a model look artificially accurate.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Tasks**\n",
    "20. Inspect the columns for anything that looks like it could only be known after a customer has already churned, or that is purely an identifier. List any suspects and explain your reasoning.\n",
    "21. In 2–3 sentences, explain what would go wrong if such a column were left in the model's input features."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Task 20 — Check for data leakage\nprint(\"=\"*70)\nprint(\"DATA LEAKAGE INSPECTION\")\nprint(\"=\"*70)\n",
    "\nprint(\"\"\"\nCHECKLIST FOR EACH COLUMN:\n\"\"\")\n\nfor col in clean_df.columns:\n    print(f\"\\n{col}:\")\n    print(\"-\" * 70)\n    \n    if col == 'Churn':\n        print(\"✅ TARGET VARIABLE - Keep for training\")\n    elif col in ['customerID']:\n        print(\"⚠️ IDENTIFIER - Should be dropped (no predictive value)\")\n    elif col == 'tenure':\n        print(\"✅ SAFE - Available at prediction time (customer tenure is known)\")\n    elif col in ['MonthlyCharges', 'TotalCharges']:\n        print(\"✅ SAFE - Available at prediction time (billing information is known)\")\n    elif col in ['gender', 'SeniorCitizen', 'Partner', 'Dependents']:\n        print(\"✅ SAFE - Demographics available at prediction time\")\n    elif col in ['PhoneService', 'InternetService', 'OnlineSecurity', 'OnlineBackup', \n                  'DeviceProtection', 'TechSupport', 'StreamingTV', 'StreamingMovies',\n                  'Contract', 'PaperlessBilling', 'PaymentMethod']:\n        print(\"✅ SAFE - Current service configuration available at prediction time\")\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*70)\nprint(\"LEAKAGE RISK ASSESSMENT\")\nprint(\"=\"*70)\n\nprint(\"\"\"\n✅ SAFE TO USE - No detected data leakage!\n\nAll features represent information that would be available at prediction time:\n- Demographics (gender, age, family status) ✅\n- Customer account history (tenure, contract type) ✅  \n- Current services (internet, security, streaming subscriptions) ✅\n- Billing information (charges, payment method) ✅\n\n❌ UNSAFE (would be removed before modeling):\n- customerID (if present) - pure identifier, no predictive value\n\nCONCLUSION: Dataset is ready for ML modeling with no leakage concerns!\n\"\"\")"
   ]
