    "- **Services** (internet type, subscriptions): Current service status known\n",
    "- **Billing** (charges, payment method): Known from account history\n",
    "- **Tenure**: Customer account age is historical fact\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer 21 (what would go wrong if leakage existed):**\n",
    "\n",
    "If a leaky feature existed (e.g., \"reason for cancellation\" that's only available after churn), the model would learn a spurious relationship and report artificially high accuracy during training, but fail catastrophically in production where that information is unavailable. The model would appear to predict churn perfectly during development but have zero predictive power in the real world, leading to wrong business decisions and wasted retention resources."
